lisa-design:
- SUPERSEDES the R34 note "Everything else file-origin is fatal, including env-location and negative verbosity": owner review of #95 (2026-09-30) overrode it. File-origin `verbosity < 0` (hclog Warn) and `${env:}` outside plugins.*.config (labels, policy_data, ...; not policy_bundles, a new feature) are WARN-ONLY: reported in `warnings`, value kept unchanged, plugin NOT skipped. Overlay-origin stays strict. The skip class stays exactly /plugins/<p>/schedule.
- R60 (owner decision 2026-09-30): a file-origin unset ${env:X} in plugins.*.config is a warning (FieldCodeEnvMissing in Report.warnings) and the literal value is passed through unchanged, as on main. File-origin is per (pointer, variable): the base's value at that pointer references X. Overlay-introduced unset variables still fail with failed/env-missing.
- A candidate whose identity equals the running one is ADOPTED in place (no restart): the running runtime keeps its pointer, its syncMeta (atomic) gets the new applied revision, and rc.active/rc.pending are replaced by a record with the new base/overlay so sameAsActive holds. Inline test runs compile under SandboxCapabilities with denied builtins rewritten to an erroring stub; Check returns before tests when a denied builtin is reachable.
